hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24336","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, that he said: He asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Are we better or those after us, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If one of them spent Uhud in gold, it would not reach the mudd of one of you, nor half of it."
"24337","Muhammad ibn Kunasah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Haytham al-Attar narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named me Yusuf and seated me in his lap."
"24338","Waki' narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Haytham al-Attar narrated to us, who said: I heard Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named me and wiped over my head."
"24339","Waki' narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Qays, who said: I heard Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named me Yusuf."
